(* Content-type: application/vnd.wolfram.mathematica *)

(*** Wolfram Notebook File ***)
(* http://www.wolfram.com/nb *)

(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Checks of the manipulations up to equation (15)", "Title"],
Cell["Companion to Research_Journal_Acoustic_Expander_10_Tout (the version with the outflow at T_out = Tbar (P*/Pbar)^eps, P* = P_out + dP_max/3). Every algebraic step of sections 1 to 5.1 is redone here with the symbols of the note and compared with the expression the note gives; a check returns True (or the difference simplifies to 0). The numbers quoted in the text are recomputed from the notebooks' constants in the last section. Evaluate the notebook top to bottom; the final cell lists all checks.", "Text"],
Cell["Symbols: cp, cv, R, gam (gamma), P, V, M, T, Tin, Tout, Fin, Fout (the flows), A, m, b (piston), Pb = Pbar, Vb = Vbar_cv, Vp = Vbar_pass, p1 = P', x1 = x', xd1 = dx'/dt, Vbd = dVbar_cv/dt, mbi, mbo = mdot_bar_in, mdot_bar_out, mi1, mo1 = d mdot_in/dP', d mdot_out/dP', e = bookkeeping parameter for the order in the fluctuations. En is the energy (E is reserved in Mathematica).", "Text"],
Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\nchecks = {};\nnote[name_, result_] := (AppendTo[checks, {name, result}]; result);", "Input"],
Cell["Section 1: the reed law (6)", "Section"],
Cell["The shape of (6) is (1 - u) Sqrt[u]. Its maximum is at u = 1/3, which is where (10b) puts P* = P_out + dP_max/3, and c1 = 3 Sqrt[3]/2 makes the peak flow equal to mdot_max.", "Text"],
Cell["flow[u_] := (1 - u) Sqrt[u];\nuPeak = u /. First[Solve[D[flow[u], u] == 0, u]];\nsecondDerivativeAtPeak = (D[flow[u], {u, 2}] /. u -> uPeak);\nc1 = 3 Sqrt[3]/2;\nnote[\"(6): the flow peaks at u = 1/3\", uPeak == 1/3 && Simplify[secondDerivativeAtPeak < 0]]\nnote[\"(6): c1 (1 - 1/3) Sqrt[1/3] = 1, so the peak flow is mdot_max\", Simplify[c1 flow[1/3]] == 1]", "Input"],
Cell["Section 2: the model as one pressure equation", "Section"],
Cell["(3) gives M T = P V/R and E = (cv/R) P V. Differentiate, insert into (2), collect the P dV/dt terms with 1 + cv/R = cp/R and multiply by R/(cv V) with (R/cv) cp = gamma R. Both identities need R = cp - cv (the note's assumption; with the notebooks' constants, R = 287 and cp - cv = 306, the two coefficients are cp R/cv and 1 + R/cv instead, the Cf and gamma_E of the simulation notebooks).", "Text"],
Cell["En = cv P[t] V[t]/R;                                   (* E = cv M T with M T = P V/R *)\neq2 = D[En, t] == -P[t] D[V[t], t] + cp (Fin Tin - Fout T);        (* equation (2) *)\npdot = First[P'[t] /. Solve[eq2, P'[t]]];\neq7 = (gam R/V[t]) (Fin Tin - Fout T) - gam (P[t]/V[t]) V'[t];      (* equation (7) *)\nnote[\"(7) follows from (2) and (3) when R = cp - cv, gamma = cp/cv\",\n  Simplify[(pdot - eq7) /. {gam -> cp/cv, R -> cp - cv}] == 0]\ngeneralForm = Collect[pdot, {Fin, Fout, V'[t]}, Simplify]\nnote[\"(7) in general: flux coefficient cp R/cv, work coefficient 1 + R/cv\",\n  Simplify[pdot - ((cp R/(cv V[t])) (Fin Tin - Fout T) - (1 + R/cv) (P[t]/V[t]) V'[t])] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["(8): with no enthalpy flow, dP/P = -gamma dV/V, i.e. P V^gamma = const.", "Text"],
Cell["isentropic = (eq7 /. {Fin -> 0, Fout -> 0});\nnote[\"(8): Pdot/P = -gamma Vdot/V without enthalpy flow\", Simplify[isentropic/P[t] + gam V'[t]/V[t]] == 0]\nnote[\"(8): then d(P V^gamma)/dt = 0\", Simplify[D[P[t] V[t]^gam, t] /. P'[t] -> -gam P[t] V'[t]/V[t]] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["Section 4: one sealed cycle", "Section"],
Cell["(10): expand (Pb + P')(Vb + V')^gamma = Pb Vb^gamma to first order; with V' = A x' this is P' = -(kcv/A) x', kcv = gamma Pb A^2/Vb, and the force A P' = -kcv x' is a spring. (11): the amplitudes are related by delta = kcv a/A.", "Text"],
Cell["lin10 = Normal[Series[(Pb + e p1) (Vb + e v1)^gam - Pb Vb^gam, {e, 0, 1}]];\nnote[\"(10): first order of (P V^gamma) = const is P'/Pb + gamma V'/Vb = 0\",\n  Simplify[lin10/(e Pb Vb^gam) - (p1/Pb + gam v1/Vb)] == 0]\nkcv = gam Pb A^2/Vb;\np1of = (p1 /. First[Solve[lin10 == 0, p1]]) /. v1 -> A x1;\nnote[\"(10): P' = -(kcv/A) x' with kcv = gamma Pb A^2/Vb\", Simplify[p1of + kcv x1/A] == 0]\nnote[\"(10): the force A P' = -kcv x'\", Simplify[A p1of + kcv x1] == 0]\nnote[\"(11): delta = kcv a/A (magnitudes of (10))\",\n  Simplify[Abs[p1of] - kcv Abs[x1]/A, Assumptions -> {A > 0, Pb > 0, Vb > 0, gam > 0}] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["The passive spring: linearize (5), P_pass(x) = Pp0 (V0p/(V0p - A x))^gamma, about the mean position xb. The force of the passive side on the piston is -A P_pass, so its stiffness is A dP_pass/dx = gamma Pbar_pass A^2/Vbar_pass. (12): the piston between the two springs oscillates at omega = Sqrt[(kcv + kpass)/m], and with Pbar_pass = Pbar this is the second form of (12).", "Text"],
Cell["Ppass[x_] := Pp0 (V0p/(V0p - A x))^gam;\nkpassDef = gam Ppass[xb] A^2/(V0p - A xb);                      (* gamma Pbar_pass A^2/Vbar_pass *)\nnote[\"kpass = gamma Pbar_pass A^2/Vbar_pass from (5)\", Simplify[A Ppass'[xb] - kpassDef] == 0]\nkpass = gam Pb A^2/Vp;                                           (* with Pbar_pass = Pbar, Vbar_pass = Vp *)\nomega12 = A Sqrt[(gam Pb/m) (1/Vb + 1/Vp)];\nnote[\"(12): Sqrt[(kcv + kpass)/m] = A Sqrt[(gamma Pb/m)(1/Vb + 1/Vp)] (both positive, so compare the squares)\",\n  Simplify[(kcv + kpass)/m - omega12^2] == 0]\npistonEq = m x''[t] + b x'[t] - (-(kcv/A) x[t] - (kpass/A) x[t]) A;   (* (4) with P' and P'_pass from the two springs *)\nnote[\"(12): x = Cos[omega t] solves the undamped piston equation\",\n  Simplify[(pistonEq /. {b -> 0, x -> (Cos[omega12 #] &)}), Assumptions -> {A > 0, Pb > 0, Vb > 0, Vp > 0, gam > 0, m > 0}] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["(10a): along the sealed cycle P V^gamma = const and P V = M R T with M constant, so T/Tb = (P/Pb)^eps with eps = (gamma - 1)/gamma, and to first order T'/Tb = eps P'/Pb.", "Text"],
Cell["Vof[P_] := Vb (Pb/P)^(1/gam);                                    (* P V^gamma = Pb Vb^gamma *)\nTof[P_] := P Vof[P]/(M R);                                       (* P V = M R T *)\nTb = Tof[Pb];\neps = (gam - 1)/gam;\nnote[\"(10a): T/Tb = (P/Pb)^eps, eps = (gamma - 1)/gamma (checked on the logarithms)\",\n  Simplify[PowerExpand[Log[Tof[P]/Tb] - eps Log[P/Pb]], Assumptions -> {P > 0, Pb > 0, gam > 0}] == 0]\nnote[\"(10a): first order T'/Tb = eps P'/Pb\",\n  Simplify[PowerExpand[Normal[Series[Tof[Pb + p1]/Tb, {p1, 0, 1}]]] - (1 + eps p1/Pb), Assumptions -> {Pb > 0, gam > 0}] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["The notebooks' constants (R = 287, cv = 744, cp = 1050, gamma = 1.41) do not satisfy R = cp - cv. With E = cv M T and P V = M R T, a sealed cycle (dE = -P dV) gives T V^(R/cv) = const and P V^(1 + R/cv) = const, so d ln T/d ln P = R/(cv + R) = 0.2784 instead of (gamma - 1)/gamma = 0.2908; this is the exponent the note uses for its numbers.", "Text"],
Cell["Tv[v_] := T0 (V0/v)^(R/cv); Pv[v_] := M R Tv[v]/v;\nnote[\"sealed cycle with E = cv M T: dE/dV = -P holds for T ~ V^(-R/cv)\", Simplify[cv M D[Tv[v], v] + Pv[v]] == 0]\nnote[\"then d ln T/d ln P = R/(cv + R)\", Simplify[D[Log[Tv[v]], v]/D[Log[Pv[v]], v] - R/(cv + R)] == 0]\n{N[287/(744 + 287)], N[(1.41 - 1)/1.41]}", "Input"],
Cell["(10b) is a definition: T_out = Tb (P*/Pb)^eps with P* = P_out + dP_max/3, the peak of (6) (section 1 above). Its numbers are in the last section.", "Text"],
Cell["Section 5.1: the tangent slope", "Section"],
Cell["(13a): T_out depends on the mean state only, so the product mdot_out T_out has no term in T'.", "Text"],
Cell["note[\"(13a): (mbo + mo1 P') Tout = mbo Tout + Tout mo1 P'\", Expand[(mbo + mo1 p1) Tout - (mbo Tout + Tout mo1 p1)] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["Substitute P = Pb + P', V = Vb + A x', dV/dt = dVb/dt + A dx'/dt, the flows (13) and (13a), and 1/V = (1/Vb)(1 - A x'/Vb + ...) into (7), and sort by order in the fluctuations (the bookkeeping parameter e). Order 0 is the purely slow part, order 1 the oscillating part linear in one fluctuation, order 2 the quadratic terms.", "Text"],
Cell["Pf = Pb + e p1; Vf = Vb + e A x1; Vdf = Vbd + e A xd1;\nminf = mbi + e mi1 p1; moutf = mbo + e mo1 p1;                 (* (13) *)\nrhs7 = (gam R/Vf) (minf Tin - moutf Tout) - gam (Pf/Vf) Vdf;     (* (7) with the outflow at Tout *)\nser = Series[rhs7, {e, 0, 2}];\nslow = SeriesCoefficient[ser, 0]; lin = SeriesCoefficient[ser, 1]; quad = SeriesCoefficient[ser, 2];\nnote[\"5.1: the purely slow part is (gamma R/Vb)(Tin mbi - Tout mbo) - (gamma Pb/Vb) dVb/dt\",\n  Simplify[slow - ((gam R/Vb) (Tin mbi - Tout mbo) - gam Pb Vbd/Vb)] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["The oscillating part linear in one fluctuation, as the note writes it: the gas spring, the valve term, and a bracket of two slow-rate terms. The expansion produces one more term of the same kind in the bracket, + gamma (Pb dVb/dt/Vb^2) V', from the product of 1/V's oscillatory part with the mean work term; it is as small as the other two (numbers in the last section) and is dropped with them. The check below shows the difference.", "Text"],
Cell["Sb = Tin mbi - Tout mbo; V1 = A x1;\nnoteLin = -(gam Pb A/Vb) xd1 + (gam R/Vb) (Tin mi1 - Tout mo1) p1 + (-(gam R/Vb^2) Sb V1 - gam (Vbd/Vb) p1);\nthirdTerm = Simplify[lin - noteLin]\nnote[\"5.1: the linear oscillating part is the note's expression plus gamma (Pb Vbd/Vb^2) V'\",\n  Simplify[lin - noteLin - gam Pb Vbd V1/Vb^2] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["With V' = -(Vb/(gamma Pb)) P' from (10) and Sb ~ Tb mdot_net, the three bracket terms are [mdot_net/Mb - gamma (dVb/dt)/Vb - (dVb/dt)/Vb] P': fractional rates of change of the mean mass and the mean volume.", "Text"],
Cell["bracket3 = (-(gam R/Vb^2) Sb V1 - gam (Vbd/Vb) p1 + gam Pb Vbd V1/Vb^2) /. {x1 -> -(Vb/(gam Pb A)) p1, mbi -> mnet + mbo, Tin -> Tm, Tout -> Tm};\nnote[\"5.1: the bracket is [mdot_net/Mb - gamma Vbd/Vb - Vbd/Vb] P' with Mb = Pb Vb/(R Tm), Tm the mean temperature\",\n  Simplify[bracket3/p1 - (R Tm mnet/(Pb Vb) - gam Vbd/Vb - Vbd/Vb)] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["The quadratic terms are products of two first harmonics, which contain only a constant and a second harmonic: with P' = delta Cos[psi], x' ~ Cos[psi], dx'/dt ~ Sin[psi] nothing at the fundamental is left.", "Text"],
Cell["quad\nquadHarmonics = TrigReduce[quad /. {p1 -> dl Cos[psi], x1 -> a Cos[psi], xd1 -> -a om Sin[psi]}];\nnote[\"5.1: the quadratic terms have no first harmonic\", FreeQ[quadHarmonics, Cos[psi] | Sin[psi]]]", "Input"],
Cell["(14): with gamma Pb A/Vb = kcv/A the gas-spring term is -(kcv/A) dx'/dt, and g is the coefficient of P'. The chain rule turns the slopes with respect to P' into the slope of the reed law at the mean drop: mdot_in = mdot(P_in - P) gives d mdot_in/dP' = -mdot'(dPbar_in), mdot_out = mdot(P - P_out) gives +mdot'(dPbar_out).", "Text"],
Cell["note[\"(14): gamma Pb A/Vb = kcv/A\", Simplify[gam Pb A/Vb - kcv/A] == 0]\ngdef = (gam R/Vb) (Tin mi1 - Tout mo1);\nnote[\"(14): the linear part without the bracket is -(kcv/A) x'dot + g P'\",\n  Simplify[(lin - (-(gam R/Vb^2) Sb V1 - gam (Vbd/Vb) p1 + gam Pb Vbd V1/Vb^2)) - (-(kcv/A) xd1 + gdef p1)] == 0]\ndmin = D[mdot[Pin - (Pb + p1)], p1] /. p1 -> 0;                  (* d mdot_in/dP' at the mean *)\ndmout = D[mdot[(Pb + p1) - Pout], p1] /. p1 -> 0;                (* d mdot_out/dP' at the mean *)\nnote[\"(14): d mdot_in/dP' = -mdot'(Pin - Pb), d mdot_out/dP' = +mdot'(Pb - Pout)\",\n  Simplify[dmin + mdot'[Pin - Pb]] == 0 && Simplify[dmout - mdot'[Pb - Pout]] == 0]\ng14 = -(gam R/Vb) (Tin mdot'[Pin - Pb] + Tout mdot'[Pb - Pout]);\nnote[\"(14): g = -(gamma R/Vb)(Tin mdot'_in + Tout mdot'_out)\",\n  Simplify[(gdef /. {mi1 -> dmin, mo1 -> dmout}) - g14] == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["(15): the slope of the reed law (6), mdot'(dP) = (c1 mdot_max/dP_max) (1 - 3u)/(2 Sqrt[u]); negative on the falling branch 1/3 < u < 1, positive on 0 < u < 1/3.", "Text"],
Cell["mdotLaw[dP_] := c1 mmax (1 - dP/dPmax) Sqrt[dP/dPmax];\nslope15 = (c1 mmax/dPmax) (1 - 3 u)/(2 Sqrt[u]) /. u -> dP/dPmax;\nnote[\"(15): d mdot/d(dP) = (c1 mdot_max/dP_max)(1 - 3u)/(2 Sqrt[u])\",\n  Simplify[D[mdotLaw[dP], dP] - slope15, Assumptions -> {dP > 0, dPmax > 0}] == 0]\nnote[\"(15): negative on the falling branch 1/3 < u < 1, positive on 0 < u < 1/3, zero at u = 1/3\",\n  Resolve[ForAll[u, 1/3 < u < 1, (1 - 3 u)/(2 Sqrt[u]) < 0], Reals] &&\n  Resolve[ForAll[u, 0 < u < 1/3, (1 - 3 u)/(2 Sqrt[u]) > 0], Reals] && ((1 - 3 u)/(2 Sqrt[u]) /. u -> 1/3) == 0]", "Input"],
Cell["The numbers quoted in sections 3 to 5.1 (baseline of the sweep notebooks)", "Section"],
Cell["Constants of the simulation notebooks. c1 mdot_max of (6) is the m_max = 0.001 kg/s of the code, dP_max = (P_in - P_out)/(2 zeta), and the adiabatic exponent is R/(cv + R) (see section 4 above). At t = 0 the piston is at x = 0, so Vbar_cv = V0c.", "Text"],
Cell["base = {gam -> 1.41, R -> 287., cp -> 1050., cv -> 744., Pin -> 6.0 10^5, Pout -> 5.45 10^5, P0 -> 5.75 10^5, Tin -> 300.,\n   A -> 2.85 10^-4, m -> 1.5 10^-3, b -> 0.005, zeta -> 0.6, mmax -> 0.001, V0p -> 2.0 10^-4, V0c -> 1.0 10^-4};\ndPmaxN = (Pin - Pout)/(2 zeta) /. base;\nepsN = R/(cv + R) /. base;\nPstarN = (Pout /. base) + dPmaxN/3;\nthetaOf[Pbar_] := (PstarN/Pbar)^epsN;\nPb0 = 5.725 10^5;                                                  (* the steady mean pressure, P_b = (P_in + P_out)/2 *)\nf0 = (A Sqrt[(gam P0/m) (1/V0c + 1/V0p)] /. base)/(2 Pi);          (* (12) at the start: 129 Hz, the 100 to 130 Hz of section 3 *)\nGrid[{{\"dP_max [bar]\", dPmaxN/10^5}, {\"eps = R/(cv + R)\", epsN}, {\"P* [bar]\", PstarN/10^5}, {\"f0 [Hz] from (12)\", f0},\n  {\"(P*/Pb)^eps at the steady mean\", thetaOf[Pb0]}, {\"Tbar - Tout at the steady mean [K], Tbar = 300 K\", 300 (1 - thetaOf[Pb0])},\n  {\"the same at the simulated mean 5.716 bar, Tbar = 299.2 K\", 299.2 (1 - thetaOf[5.716 10^5])},\n  {\"Tbar - Tout at Pbar = P_in [K]\", 300 (1 - thetaOf[Pin /. base])},\n  {\"eps Tbar delta/Pbar at the steady swing [K] (section 4)\", epsN 299. 0.2946/5.725}}, Alignment -> Left]", "Input"],
Cell["Section 5.1 after (14): (P*/Pbar)^eps at the start of the baseline, the outlet's share of the valve gain, and what T_out does to g. The valve gain g at delta -> 0 is (14) with (15); c1 mdot_max = m_max of the code.", "Text"],
Cell["uin = (Pin - P0)/dPmaxN /. base; uout = (P0 - Pout)/dPmaxN /. base;\nsl[u_] := (1 - 3 u)/(2 Sqrt[u]);                                  (* (15) in units of c1 mdot_max/dP_max *)\ngBar = -(gam R Tin/V0c) (mmax/dPmaxN) (sl[uin] + sl[uout]) /. base;\ngOut = -(gam R Tin/V0c) (mmax/dPmaxN) (sl[uin] + thetaOf[P0] sl[uout]) /. base;\nGrid[{{\"(P*/P0)^eps at the start\", thetaOf[P0 /. base]}, {\"1 - (P*/P0)^eps [%]\", 100 (1 - thetaOf[P0 /. base])},\n  {\"outlet share of the valve gain\", sl[uout]/(sl[uin] + sl[uout])}, {\"g with Tbar at the outlet [1/s]\", gBar},\n  {\"g with Tout [1/s]\", gOut}, {\"change [1/s]\", gOut - gBar}, {\"change [%]\", 100 (gOut - gBar)/gBar},\n  {\"eps dP_max/P0\", epsN dPmaxN/(P0 /. base)}, {\"P0/dP_max\", (P0 /. base)/dPmaxN}}, Alignment -> Left]", "Input"],
Cell["The size of the dropped bracket (section 5.1): the three slow rates against the valve rate. The mean-pressure drift at the start is mdot_net/C with C = (V0c + V0p)/(gamma R Tin) (this is (31) of section 9, used only for the number), and dVbar_cv/dt = (Vbar_pass/(gamma Pbar)) dPbar/dt from (25).", "Text"],
Cell["mnetN = mmax (flow[uin] - flow[uout]) /. base;                     (* net inflow at P0, kg/s *)\nM0 = P0 V0c/(R Tin) /. base;\nCdrift = (V0c + V0p)/(gam R Tin) /. base;\nVbdN = (V0p/(gam P0)) (mnetN/Cdrift) /. base;\nGrid[{{\"mdot_net at P0 [g/s]\", 1000 mnetN}, {\"M0 [g]\", 1000 M0}, {\"mdot_net/M [1/s]\", mnetN/M0},\n  {\"gamma Vbdot/Vb [1/s]\", gam VbdN/V0c /. base}, {\"Vbdot/Vb [1/s] (the third term)\", VbdN/V0c /. base},\n  {\"bracket total [1/s]\", mnetN/M0 - (gam VbdN/V0c /. base) - (VbdN/V0c /. base)},\n  {\"valve rate (gamma R/Vb) d mdot/dP' [1/s]\", gBar},\n  {\"gamma (c1 mdot_max/M)(P0/dP_max) [1/s], the estimate of 5.1\", gam (mmax/M0) (P0/dPmaxN) /. base}}, Alignment -> Left]", "Input"],
Cell["All checks", "Section"],
Cell["TableForm[checks]\nnote[\"ALL\", And @@ (Last /@ checks)]", "Input"]
},
WindowSize->{1100, 850},
WindowMargins->{{Automatic, Automatic}, {Automatic, Automatic}},
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
